2026-09-02 (later)  The ambient check on real data: no verdict, and why
================================================================================
Withdrawn:
  - The earlier "+1.00 K, not suspect" on the SINTEF record. delta_theta_or had
    been fitted on the same record the check was then applied to. Least squares
    zeroes the mean residual on its own fitting subset, so the number was an
    artefact of subset selection rather than a statement about the probe.
    EVIDENCE.md claim 119 is marked withdrawn rather than edited away.
What a proper run shows:
  - Break the circularity with a time split and the VERDICT FLIPS. Fit on the
    first half, check the second: +1.39 K, suspect. Reverse it: +0.48 K, not
    suspect. The halves disagree on the rated oil rise by 2.20 K, which is the
    honest measure of how weakly a 0.048-0.429 pu hull constrains a rated value.
  - The offset passes only at the loss ratio we assumed. Sweeping R from 4 to 10
    moves it +3.64 -> -3.12 K, changing sign. R is not supplied with the dataset.
    On this record the mean offset reads out our assumption, not the probe.
  - The residual is not flat. Day-night swing 2.99 K (day -1.50, night +1.48)
    against a mean of +0.01 K, with the sign a sun-exposed probe would give --
    but confounded with oil thermal lag, because the quasi-steady test
    constrains LOAD stability and not AMBIENT stability. Not attributable.
    Monthly residual swings 2.5 K, mechanism not established, and explicitly NOT
    the oil-viscosity effect, which would act in the opposite direction.
About the check itself:
  - An ONAN unit has no cooling stages, so the stage-split diagnostic -- the
    sharper of the check's two axes -- is unavailable, leaving only the mean.
    That is the statistic most contaminated by model error, as the R sweep shows.
  - (c) Proposed, not built: a diurnal-component axis for stageless units. It
    needs the oil lag handled first or it will report thermal inertia as probe
    error.
No code changed in this entry. Suite unchanged at 259.

